# CSS Design System

Full conventions are in `/.cursor/docs/css.md`. Key rules below.

## Tokens — Never Hardcode Values

All design tokens live in `:root`. Never use raw hex, px shadow, or border values outside `:root`.

| Prefix | Example |
| --- | --- |
| `--color-primary-*` | `--color-primary-500: #f97316` |
| `--color-neutral-*` | `--color-neutral-900: #18181b` |
| `--color-status-*` | `--color-status-red/green/orange/neutral` |
| `--size-*` | `--size-16: 1rem` (named after px equivalent) |
| `--border-radius-*` | `--border-radius-1/2/3/round` |
| `--shadow-*` | `--shadow-1` (outermost) → lighter per inner layer |

## Semantic Theme Layer

Use `--theme-*` tokens for any value that differs between light and dark mode. Never use `--color-*` tokens directly in component rules where theming applies.

**Available tokens:**

| Token | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `--theme-logo` | SVG logo fill |
| `--theme-container-0` | Page background |
| `--theme-container-1` | Outermost card background (gradient) |
| `--theme-container-2` | Inner panel background (gradient) |
| `--theme-container-3` | Innermost panel background (gradient) |
| `--theme-container-4` | Input / select / pill surface fill |
| `--theme-container-border` | Gradient border for containers 1–3 |
| `--theme-container-4-border` | Solid border for container-4 / inputs |
| `--theme-text` | Primary body text |
| `--theme-text-faded` | Secondary / muted text, labels |

**Three override layers — always set `color-scheme` alongside the tokens:**

```css
/* :root sets light defaults */
:root { color-scheme: light; --theme-text: var(--color-neutral-600); /* ... */ }

/* System preference */
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root { color-scheme: dark; --theme-text: var(--color-neutral-300); /* ... */ }
}

/* Manual overrides — JS sets document.documentElement.dataset.theme */
[data-theme="dark"]  { color-scheme: dark;  --theme-text: var(--color-neutral-300); /* ... */ }
[data-theme="light"] { color-scheme: light; --theme-text: var(--color-neutral-600); /* ... */ }
```

`color-scheme` tells the browser which scheme to use for native UI (scrollbars, form controls) so they match the active theme. Never toggle dark-mode classes — JS only writes `data-theme`.

## Naming — BEM-lite, Kebab-case

```
.block {}
.block-element {}
.block-modifier {}
.block-element-modifier {}
```

- Always kebab-case. No camelCase, PascalCase, or underscores.
- Single dashes only — no double dashes.
- Numbered tiers for structural depth: `.container-1`, `.container-2`, `.container-3`

## Containers

Each tier maps to a matching radius, shadow, and gradient-border background:

```css
.container-1 { border-radius: var(--border-radius-1); box-shadow: var(--shadow-1); }
.container-2 { border-radius: var(--border-radius-2); }
.container-3 { border-radius: var(--border-radius-3); }
```

Gradient borders use a two-layer `background`: `padding-box` fill + `border-box` gradient, with `border-color: transparent`. Never use `border-image` alongside `border-radius` — they are incompatible.

## Property Order (within a rule)

1. Positioning (`position`, `top`, `z-index`)
2. Display & layout (`display`, `flex-*`, `grid-*`, `align-*`, `justify-*`)
3. Box model (`width`, `height`, `padding`, `margin`, `border`, `border-radius`)
4. Typography (`font-*`, `line-height`, `text-*`, `letter-spacing`)
5. Visual (`color`, `background`, `box-shadow`, `opacity`, `overflow`)
6. Interaction (`cursor`, `pointer-events`, `transition`, `transform`)

Always list explicit properties in `transition` — never `transition: all`.

## State — JS Sets ARIA, CSS Reads It

| State | JS sets | CSS selector |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Validation error | `aria-invalid="true"` | `input[aria-invalid="true"]` |
| Toggle active | `aria-pressed="true"` | `.toggle[aria-pressed="true"]` |
| Active tab | `aria-selected="true"` | `.tab[aria-selected="true"]` |
| Theme | `data-theme="dark"` | `[data-theme="dark"]` |
| Collapsible open | native `[open]` | `.collapsible[open]` |

Never add/remove CSS classes for state that ARIA attributes or `[open]` already track.

## Component Patterns

**Collapsible** — `<details>`/`<summary>` with `::details-content` animation (`block-size`, `opacity`, `content-visibility`). Icon rotation is purely CSS: `.collapsible[open] .collapsible-toggle-icon { transform: rotate(45deg); }` — no JS class toggle.

**Toast** — `.message` base + `.success / .error / .loading` variants. Use `role="status" aria-live="polite"` for confirmations; `role="alert"` for errors. `pointer-events: none` on the base; re-enable on active variants.

**Toggle switch** — native `<input type="checkbox" role="switch">` visually hidden; track/thumb styled via sibling `+` and `:checked` selectors. No JS needed for visuals.

**Select** — `appearance: none` with a custom chevron injected via `background` shorthand (SVG `url()` + container color).

## File Structure & Responsive

Sections in order: imports → `:root` → body → nav/layout → typography → form controls → icons → buttons → components → feature-specific → media queries.

All `@media` blocks go at the **bottom** of the file — never inline inside a component. Desktop-first using `max-width`:

| Name | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Small | `max-width: 768px` |
| XSmall | `max-width: 520px` |
| XXSmall | `max-width: 400px` |

Only override properties that genuinely differ at each breakpoint.
